# Files permitted to name the product. Format: path  # reason
#
# There are exactly two legitimate reasons to name it in this repository:
#   (a) the document RESERVES the claims — naming them is what the file is for;
#   (b) the document RECORDS the separation itself, and a record that cannot say
#       what was removed is not a record.
#
# Anything else is a leak. When this list grows, ask which of the two it is; if the
# answer takes more than a sentence, it is neither.

PATENTS.md              # Reserves the product meal score and the private weighted composite OUT of the Apache-2.0 §3 patent grant. It has to name them to except them.
PROPRIETARY_IP.md       # The forbidden/allowed list itself. Naming the artefacts is the entire function of the document.
NOTICE                  # Legal notice accompanying the licence; carries the same reservation.
LICENSE-SAMPLES.md      # Sample-data licence carve-out, same reservation.
CHANGELOG.md            # Records the separation audit — what was removed, and when. A changelog that cannot name what it removed is useless.
design/BASELINE.md      # The separation-audit starting position, including the baseline grep command and its hit counts. This is the evidence the audit happened.
design/DIVERGENCES.md   # Records renames such as KIBO_PRODUCT_SCORE_MODULE -> BAC_SCORER_MODULE. The before-column is the point.
tools/check_separation.py  # This gate. It must contain the patterns it searches for; a gate that cannot name its target cannot run.
tests/test_gates_can_fail.py  # Mutation tests for this gate. A test that cannot name the target cannot prove the gate refuses it — the same reason the gate itself is on this list. Fixtures only; no shipped code.
